# Docker build context excludes. Keeps the image lean and the build
# reproducible: host node_modules, build artifacts, secrets, VCS, and tests
# never enter the image. The Dockerfile rebuilds the web bundle and installs
# fresh deps from the lockfile.

# Dependencies — reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile.
**/node_modules

# Build artifacts — the web bundle is rebuilt in the build stage; the Prisma
# client is regenerated in each image stage.
**/dist
**/build
**/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/api/src/generated

# Secrets — never bake env into the image; prod uses env_file at runtime.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# VCS + tooling
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Tests — not needed at runtime. Excluding *.test.tsx alongside the test/
# setup dir keeps them consistent: the web build's `tsc --noEmit` fails if
# test files enter the context without src/test/setup.ts's jest-dom types.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/test
**/coverage

# Editor / OS cruft
.idea
.vscode
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Docker + compose files themselves
**/Dockerfile
**/.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
